    <briefdescription>
<para>A class that ensures a function is executed only once for a given set of arguments (including none). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="classcuda_1_1experimental_1_1stf_1_1run__once" kindref="compound">run_once</ref></computeroutput> class is a utility that caches the result of a function call based on its arguments, ensuring that the function is only run once for each unique set of arguments. It is particularly useful in scenarios where a function call is expensive and the result is invariant for the same input parameters.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Ts</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Types of the arguments used to uniquely identify the function call. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
